                  <article class="doc">
                    <p class="skill__from">Skill · from <code>create-verification-skill</code></p>
                    <h4>Verify checkout</h4>
                    <p>
                      Drives checkout in a real browser the way a shopper does, and saves a screenshot of
                      each result as proof.
                    </p>
                    <h5>Launch</h5>
                    <p>Run <code>pnpm dev --filter checkout</code>. It is ready when port 5173 answers.</p>
                    <h5>Test cases</h5>
                    <ol class="skill__cases">
                      <li>Apple Pay shows in Safari with a card in Wallet.</li>
                      <li>The button hides where Apple Pay can’t pay.</li>
                      <li>A declined payment returns to the card form.</li>
                    </ol>
                  </article>
                </div>
                <div class="pane pane--chat">
                  <div class="chat">
                    <div class="msg msg--user">
                      Use <span class="skill__chip">$verify-checkout</span> on the Apple Pay button in #513.
                    </div>
                    <ul class="worklog">
                      <li><svg class="ico ico--xs"><use href="#i-book" /></svg><span>Skill <code>verify-checkout</code> from the engineering wiki</span></li>
                      <li><svg class="ico ico--xs"><use href="#i-terminal" /></svg><code>pnpm dev --filter checkout</code></li>
                      <li><svg class="ico ico--xs"><use href="#i-eye" /></svg><span>Drove 3 test cases in Safari</span></li>
                    </ul>
                    <div class="msg msg--agent">
                      <p>All 3 test cases pass. The button hides in Firefox, and a declined payment returns to the card form. A screenshot of each case is in the thread.</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </figure>
              </div>
              <div class="surface__desc">
                <p>
                  Ask Claude to run <code>create-verification-skill</code> on your repository. The template is
                  the starting point: Claude reads how your app starts and how to drive it, then writes a
                  skill for your app with test cases that prove it.
                </p>
                <p>
                  The skill arrives in the wiki as a change request. You read it, edit it and merge it like
                  any wiki change. After that, an agent on any task in the project can use it, and its proof
                  lands in the thread.
                </p>
                <p class="surface__note">
                  So far we have tried this with Claude.
                </p>
